      "date": "2026-05-22T11:46:04.000Z",
      "title": "New minor risk - Profit margin trend",
      "body": "The company's profit margins are lower than last year and have reduced by more than 30%. Net profit margin: 13% Last year net profit margin: 32% This is considered a minor risk. A large drop in profit margin could indicate the company does not have strong competitive advantages or it is yet to establish itself and its core business. Even if it is a well established business, this may make it a much riskier investment than one that has a combination of proven competitive advantages and a stable or growing profit margin. Currently, the following risks have been identified for the company: Major Risks Interest payments are not well covered by earnings (1.2x net interest cover). Shareholders have been substantially diluted in the past year (96% increase in shares outstanding). Revenue is less ",
